# MCSP Disassembler 0.41

Status: Constructive native disassembler experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent: ASSEMBLER-SEED-0.40

## Objective

Establish the first bounded MCSP disassembler mechanism:

    machine encoding -> MCSP structural machine description

The decoder SHALL derive the structural tuple directly from machine bytes. External disassembler text is audit evidence only.

## Qualified input

For the 0.40 realization:

    48 31 d8

the bounded decoder reconstructs:

    relation = 0x01
    width = 64
    destination-register-token = 0
    source-register-token = 3
    operand-form = register/register

The relation token inherits the 0.39 structural definition:

    00->0
    01->1
    10->1
    11->0

The mnemonic XOR is not part of the reconstructed semantic tuple.

## Rejection

Unsupported or mutated encodings SHALL be rejected.

0.41 does not guess instruction meaning from partial resemblance.

## Round trip

Within the qualified scope:

    S -> ASSEMBLE_0.40(S) -> bytes
    bytes -> DISASSEMBLE_0.41(bytes) -> S'

Pass requires S' = S for every material field admitted by the fixture.

This equality is bounded structural equality, not a claim that assembly and disassembly are universal mathematical inverses.

## Boundary

The 0.41 decoder implementation is bootstrapped in NASM but its target-byte decoding decision is internal.

General x86-64 decoding remains outside scope.
Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.
